{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540162-hypothetically-what-aid-could-the-syndicate-give-to-others-in-destroying-pentex","id":1540162,"title":"Hypothetically, what aid could the Syndicate give to others in destroying Pentex?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-08-10T19:25:29-07:00","id":1540162,"title":"Hypothetically, what aid could the Syndicate give to others in destroying Pentex?","content":"So a group of supernaturals, the Traditions or maybe even the Glass Walkers on behalf of the Garou Nation, approach the Syndicate with proof of their involvement with Pentex and demands the Syndicate's unlimited support in destroying Pentex in exchange for keeping their mouth's shut about the matter. What can the Syndicate do to help anyone interested in taking down Pentex? They seem to describe themselves to be quite powerless in this matter, IIRC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 08-10-2024, 11:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-10T20:13:37-07:00","id":1540166,"title":"","content":"Lawyers, guns, and money.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-11T04:50:15-07:00","id":1540170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540162-hypothetically-what-aid-could-the-syndicate-give-to-others-in-destroying-pentex?p=1540166#post1540166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lawyers, guns, and money.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't forget inside data. Pentex and the Syndicate were thick as thieves. The Syndicate knows almost all of Pentex's secrets and vice versa.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-11T08:39:54-07:00","id":1540173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540162-hypothetically-what-aid-could-the-syndicate-give-to-others-in-destroying-pentex?p=1540170#post1540170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't forget inside data. Pentex and the Syndicate were thick as thieves. The Syndicate knows almost all of Pentex's secrets and vice versa.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that the Syndicate seems utterly in the dark about SPD beyond &quot;it prints money!&quot;, I rather doubt that their knowledge of Pentex is that extensive. Conversely, Pentex probably has no problem finding a hole in the Syndicate (just one nephandus means that they can pay them off for info).<br /> <br /> As for what the Syndicate can do, &quot;get out of the way&quot; would top the list. Conceptually, however, this would end its existence and undermine a lot of the rest of the Technocracy, since properly getting out of the way would involve deconstructing capitalist society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-11T16:02:47-07:00","id":1540186,"title":"","content":"I second <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a>, the Syndicate as a whole wasn't all that informed about Pentex, and the part that was has defected. This is a current plot point, by the way, with at least one special ops group within the Syndicate working to find out what the hell was happening.<br /> <br /> As a whole the Syndicate can't do much more than they're already doing: be more environment friendly in their business, investigate Pentex, hunt infiltrators, none of those are easy or quick solutions. And precisely because it involves infiltrators, they can't do shit as a unified Convention, at risk of feeding vital information to the enemy.<br /> <br /> To be honest their most probable reaction would be to play nice only as they prepare the trap to catch and eliminate the party that's trying to blackmail them. That would be their top priority as far as their safety goes. They're professional conspirators, the correct answer to hostage or blackmail situations isn't ever to bite the bait and pay.<br /> <br /> Now, if this group actually approaches the Syndicate as prospective partners instead of jerks, or better, approach amenable Syndicate operatives and/or supervisor, then the best thing they can get is the direct help of one Syndicate agent or, at most, a single Syndicate-controlled amalgam.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-11T17:34:03-07:00","id":1540188,"title":"","content":"I think, if the assumption is that the PCs are the one's doing stuff, the Syndicate can actually do a whole lot more than &quot;get out of the way&quot; when it comes to aiding a group that's going after Pentex without overplaying their own hands. The biggest difficulty with Pentex is that very few people have the skill to ferret them out in the tangled web of major finance companies. The Syndicate happens to have a large number of experts on that. If the Syndicate is helping from the shadows by helping get rid of red tape, leaking documents that indicate links between companies that 99.99% of people would never figure out, etc. it can do a lot to cut through Pentex's primary defense of being hard to find in the first place.<br /> <br /> If a third party is taking down Pentex companies with some sly help from the Syndicate, it's not major threat to the Syndicate or their position in the Union (esp since it means the Syndicate knows which companies are going down and can shift markets around to avoid disruptions), and it makes a group of monkeywrenchers way more effective in the damage they can do to Pentex's real bottom line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-11T18:03:55-07:00","id":1540189,"title":"","content":"If the Syndicate is genuinely unaware of the true nature of Pentex and the SPD, I think that could actually be helpful in this scenario. I don't really imagine the Syndicate being all that vulnerable to blackmail as in the original scenario above, but if Pentex's true nature is revealed to them, they might decide to assist the PCs willingly.<br /> <br /> In that case, I think the advantage to Syndicate involvement will be to take some of Pentex's advantages against the PCs off the table. Pentex has money and connections and can target a PC in a lot of ways through financial means, social institutions and so on. But the Syndicate ALSO has money and connections, and may be able to counter Pentex's moves in that direction, leaving the PCs free to attack Pentex in a more direct, Garou-friendly way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-12T15:15:02-07:00","id":1540227,"title":"","content":"The Syndicate has to be open to accepting at least part of the explanation about Pentex. Given that even Tradition mages (and their players) are extremely quick to dismiss everything about the Garou frame of reference as superstition, I think that the effort is doomed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-12T15:42:33-07:00","id":1540231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalinara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540162-hypothetically-what-aid-could-the-syndicate-give-to-others-in-destroying-pentex?p=1540189#post1540189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Syndicate is genuinely unaware of the true nature of Pentex and the SPD, I think that could actually be helpful in this scenario. I don't really imagine the Syndicate being all that vulnerable to blackmail as in the original scenario above, but if Pentex's true nature is revealed to them, they might decide to assist the PCs willingly.<br /> <br /> In that case, I think the advantage to Syndicate involvement will be to take some of Pentex's advantages against the PCs off the table. Pentex has money and connections and can target a PC in a lot of ways through financial means, social institutions and so on. But the Syndicate ALSO has money and connections, and may be able to counter Pentex's moves in that direction, leaving the PCs free to attack Pentex in a more direct, Garou-friendly way.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Syndicate is partially aware of the true nature of Pentex, but as any Convention they're also pretty sure that they can and should solve the problem internally.<br /> <br /> And their fear that the others find out about the whole debacle is, again, an official plot point.<br /> <br /> So the Syndicate <b><u>is</u></b> aware of the problem, but <b><u>will</u></b> face any attempt at blackmail as a threat, not an opportunity. And they won't solve any threat by Reality Deviants by playing nice.<br /> <br /> Unless this group approaches a trustworthy Syndicate agent by more diplomatic means, they're just making a huge, unnecessary, enemy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-12T18:31:35-07:00","id":1540255,"title":"","content":"I'd imagine that the theoretical alliance between the player characters and the Syndicate would be an adventure in its own right. I keep imagining something like a supernatural version of Leverage, which seems like it could be a lot of fun. (And of course, if the Syndicate then becomes the direct enemy of the PCs afterward, that can make for a fun story too.)<br /> <br /> In terms of what the Syndicate can do to Pentex, if sufficiently motivated, I wish I knew more about corporate practices in general. I think they could possibly attack through governmental entities. Like the EPA, or even the Food and Drug Administration. They might be able to get certifications or permissions withdrawn. Possibly they could get different sites, like manufacturing plants, closed down or condemned as hazardous. Even if Pentex covered their tracks and did everything completely above board, the Syndicate could possibly manufacture evidence to use against them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-13T13:40:38-07:00","id":1540291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540162-hypothetically-what-aid-could-the-syndicate-give-to-others-in-destroying-pentex?p=1540231#post1540231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Syndicate is partially aware of the true nature of Pentex, but as any Convention they're also pretty sure that they can and should solve the problem internally.<br /> <br /> And their fear that the others find out about the whole debacle is, again, an official plot point.<br /> <br /> So the Syndicate <b><u>is</u></b> aware of the problem, but <b><u>will</u></b> face any attempt at blackmail as a threat, not an opportunity. And they won't solve any threat by Reality Deviants by playing nice.<br /> <br /> Unless this group approaches a trustworthy Syndicate agent by more diplomatic means, they're just making a huge, unnecessary, enemy.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, the Syndicate absolutely CAN deal with Pentex by itself.<br /> <br /> Pentex-SPD represents more or less 50% of SPD, which by itself is around 1/5 of the Syndicate itself. Therefore, we could say that the entire Pentex problem represents somewhat close to 10% of their capabilities.<br /> <br /> Now, that's not nothing - in fact, it is A LOT, but they absolutely can deal with it.<br /> <br /> And that's exactly the problem - mainly, because it ain't that huge of a problem. Because of that, this means that there are other problems that represent a bigger problem to the Syndicate.<br /> <br /> That information leaking to the other Conventions, for example, would represent a major problem to them - BIGGER than Pentex. And that would be a major destabilizing problem for the entire Technocracy.<br /> <br /> Because of that, they are trying to deal with this internally - but their main priority is NOT to root out the Pentex, but rather to not let that whole fiasco leak. Rooting out Pentex is merely their distant second priority.<br /> <br /> Over the long run, Pentex will be dismantled - but that's only over the LONG RUN. Which is frustrating to certain interested third parties that may not be as patient - and that may be suffering the consequences of the actions of Pentex. Also, while the Syndicate play their conspiracy games, all the damages caused by Pentex continue.<br /> <br /> This means that the Syndicate is proceeding extremely cautiously to the situation - one company here, one stock market crashing there, one propaganda in other place, and they are sloooooowly doing things, one piece of Intel and one lawsuit and one change of policy at a time. All for the sake of containing the threat without letting flak spill over.<br /> <br /> That's the main problem of it all. They are also not mobilizing their entire Convention to the effort - to all the other Conventions, it must seem as &quot;business as usual&quot; (pun intended), and the Syndicate has several priorities which they cannot pull from without sounding alarms. Not only that, as any good conspiracy (or in this case, a &quot;counter-conspiracy), the more people you tell &quot;the secret&quot;, the greatest danger you'll have of someone spilling their beans.<br /> <br /> They are, therefore, doing things by the books, with extremely care, with just a few select teams of trustworthy and competent personal and veeeeeery slowly. Which is frustrating. But in the long run they'll do it, but it is frustrating.<br /> <br /> Should the situation change, then all chips are off. The truth is that, for Pentex, the worse thing that they could hope for would be to be extremely successful. Because, if that were to ever happen, then the Syndicate's hand would be forced, if they perceived that the threat is getting out of control, then they would have to use brute force, since the priority would change. In that case, it would be much more likely that the Syndicate would change gears and this secret would spill over to the other Conventions, upon which at that point the full brunt of the Technocracy would be pointed at Pentex, and that would be their undoing.<br /> <br /> As it stands thou, Pentex is annoying but not an existential threat, therefore the policy of the Syndicate will remain that of cautious contending. Which may probably work on the long run, or fail and then yeah, the whole of the Union gets involved, and Pentex is purged by force. Either way, Pentex will inevitably lose, but that will take a very, very long time.<br /> <br /> If any outsider decides to try to contact the Syndicate, they may actually welcome a helping hand - and best of all, an EXTERNAL helping hand, which may give them plausible deniability. Just don't expect them to obsessively hunt the Pentex down like maniacs - they'll most likely just drip pieces of Intel here and there, and may even PROTECT Pentex assets on occasions - because remember, their priority is secrecy. Say, for instance, that blowing up a Pentex lab producing Fomori in industrial scale could potentially lead to the wrong kind of Intel falling in the leap of the NWO, than you can be damn sure that they will protect said lab from &quot;bio-terrorists&quot; with everything they have. Or a high profile Pentex Director being a target, it would raise suspiciousness if the Syndicate was not protecting that guy.<br /> <br /> Keep that in mind: while it would be highly beneficial for both parties, the Syndicate will want to do things their own way, and for their own reasons. And they won't hesitate to turn against their &quot;partners&quot; if they perceive that said alliance is bringing them more pain than it is worth it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-13T13:46:44-07:00","id":1540293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540162-hypothetically-what-aid-could-the-syndicate-give-to-others-in-destroying-pentex?p=1540227#post1540227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Syndicate has to be open to accepting at least part of the explanation about Pentex. Given that even Tradition mages (and their players) are extremely quick to dismiss everything about the Garou frame of reference as superstition, I think that the effort is doomed.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Syndicate is partly aware that Pentex (SPD) has an abnormal problem with Garous and other were-beasts. They are not dumb. They also know that this is not just a mere coincidence. What must freak them out is the thought that perhaps the Statisticians of the Iteration X or the NWO may also be wondering why the hell is that so. You can be sure that the Syndicate won't just say &quot;bah, savages&quot;. If the Garou have something to say, you can be sure that they are VERY interested in hearing, and at the very least, they would be willing to listen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-13T13:59:31-07:00","id":1540294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalinara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540162-hypothetically-what-aid-could-the-syndicate-give-to-others-in-destroying-pentex?p=1540255#post1540255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd imagine that the theoretical alliance between the player characters and the Syndicate would be an adventure in its own right. I keep imagining something like a supernatural version of Leverage, which seems like it could be a lot of fun. (And of course, if the Syndicate then becomes the direct enemy of the PCs afterward, that can make for a fun story too.)<br /> <br /> In terms of what the Syndicate can do to Pentex, if sufficiently motivated, I wish I knew more about corporate practices in general. I think they could possibly attack through governmental entities. Like the EPA, or even the Food and Drug Administration. They might be able to get certifications or permissions withdrawn. Possibly they could get different sites, like manufacturing plants, closed down or condemned as hazardous. Even if Pentex covered their tracks and did everything completely above board, the Syndicate could possibly manufacture evidence to use against them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Syndicate would appreciate to have &quot;bio-terrorists&quot; that they can &quot;direct&quot; towards the Pentex operations, while maintaining plausible deniability. That's because the Syndicate can't just simply send Enforcers to put Pentex factories to the torch - but that's where the Garou would become VERY welcomed in their plans.<br /> <br /> And yes, the Syndicate can use several institutions to strike at Pentex. But I highly doubt it would be too direct. One of the problems is that, if Pentex begins to perceive itself under attack, it will strike back. While Pentex has a lot less of capabilities then the Syndicate, they can also play the same corporate game. They can relocate operations to more &quot;friendly&quot; governments - like China for instance. And they could cut their losses, changing their markets. For instance, while the Food and Drug Administration could severely cut them in North America and Europe, they could set factories in China and export to the third world. Then, it would get far harder for the Syndicate to deal with it. Or, Pentex could change some of their operations towards the black markets, and sponsor Mexican drug cartels in the process, which would not only be harder to deal with, but it would also bring a lot of societal problems but worse of all, it could risk setting the NWO to get directly involved.<br /> <br /> One thing that Pentex can do with much more efficiency and subtlety would be markets manipulation. To cause a steadily and consistent decline in stocks from companies that are part of the Pentex group. In order to do so, the Syndicate can not only divert investment funds away from Pentex companies, but they can also invest in their direct competitors, and they can also seek to bankrupt the major suppliers of Pentex companies as well as the banks that fund them. The Syndicate can engage in a campaign of economic suffocation of the Pentex, and that's probably the best thing they can do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28035,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","user":"Magus Maximus","date":". 08-13-2024, 05:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-13T18:43:33-07:00","id":1540322,"title":"","content":"Pentex striking back would also involve waves of fomori... that conceal a type known as normalites. It might not completely freeze a mage's magickal capabilities, but they might be enough to cause horrible damage to their enlightened personnel.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540162-hypothetically-what-aid-could-the-syndicate-give-to-others-in-destroying-pentex?p=1540293#post1540293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Syndicate is partly aware that Pentex (SPD) has an abnormal problem with Garous and other were-beasts. They are not dumb. They also know that this is not just a mere coincidence. What must freak them out is the thought that perhaps the Statisticians of the Iteration X or the NWO may also be wondering why the hell is that so. You can be sure that the Syndicate won't just say &quot;bah, savages&quot;. If the Garou have something to say, you can be sure that they are VERY interested in hearing, and at the very least, they would be willing to listen.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're smart enough to realize a connection, but don't have the context or frame of mind to follow it through as far as they would need to (their particular vidare cannot conceive of itself being a vessel of the Defiler, what the Defiler properly is, or that there's something subtly different from &quot;Entropy&quot; that isn't well, and that's before we get to the animism at odds with the TU's values). Also, that would tend to go against the Syndicate's absolute info-lockdown and secrecy about the SPD problem; if they're not going to tell the other conventions, they probably aren't going to mention anything that could relate that secret to a group of Reality Deviants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-13T19:11:29-07:00","id":1540324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540162-hypothetically-what-aid-could-the-syndicate-give-to-others-in-destroying-pentex?p=1540291#post1540291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing is, the Syndicate absolutely CAN deal with Pentex by itself.<br /> <br /> Pentex-SPD represents more or less 50% of SPD, which by itself is around 1/5 of the Syndicate itself. Therefore, we could say that the entire Pentex problem represents somewhat close to 10% of their capabilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with most you said on those three posts, but I have to point some problems.<br /> <br /> First, SPD just vanished, so the Syndicate has a far deeper mystery on their hands. The whole Methodology, even the &quot;clean&quot; guys.<br /> <br /> Second, they don't know the details, because the SPD did a good job convincing people not to look, and then covering their tracks. So while the Syndicate knows Pentex is involved, they don't know how much, or in which capacity.<br /> <br /> Those are official lore. However you feel about such an obvious mess being made right under their nose, that's exactly what happened in the actual setting.<br /> <br /> Also, this is a context of conspiracies within conspiracies, and corporate politics. This reduces significantly the benefit of having greater resources. Doesn't nullify, but the outcome is far from certain.<br /> <br /> But the most glaring problem with this certainty about Syndicate victory: this is all true in a Mage game. It isn't all that clearcut in a game centered on another splat.<br /> <br /> If this is, as it seems to be the case, a WtA game, then the Technocracy is just a thing, not <b>THE </b>thing. The enemy is the Wyrm and, while not its direct servant, Pentex is the best agent of utter corruption at playing corporate conspiracy games. <br /> <br /> Nefandi are also probably a far more common thing than in the average Mage game, and even in Mage the dept of their presence within Technocratic ranks is unknown, which is another problem the Syndicate may face: it's not just those 10%.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-15T10:49:43-07:00","id":1540438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540162-hypothetically-what-aid-could-the-syndicate-give-to-others-in-destroying-pentex?p=1540322#post1540322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pentex striking back would also involve waves of fomori... that conceal a type known as normalites. It might not completely freeze a mage's magickal capabilities, but they might be enough to cause horrible damage to their enlightened personnel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Despite (probably) being a problem that the Syndicate can deal with and (perhaps) contain, the Pentex IS dangerous. I was mentioning the &quot;institutional&quot; pathways that it could use to strike back, should it saw itself being cornered. Besides those there are, quite obviously, many pathways to go into that are out of the use of societal institutions - crime and supernatural means, such as Fomori, are some of those.<br /> <br /> Pentex also has allies outside of their ranks, and potential allies, such as other Wyrm servants.<br /> <br /> For all of these reasons AND the need for keeping things rush-rush, is why the Syndicate would take baby steps towards that threat.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They're smart enough to realize a connection, but don't have the context or frame of mind to follow it through as far as they would need to (their particular vidare cannot conceive of itself being a vessel of the Defiler, what the Defiler properly is, or that there's something subtly different from &quot;Entropy&quot; that isn't well, and that's before we get to the animism at odds with the TU's values). Also, that would tend to go against the Syndicate's absolute info-lockdown and secrecy about the SPD problem; if they're not going to tell the other conventions, they probably aren't going to mention anything that could relate that secret to a group of Reality Deviants. </div> </div> </div>Sure, the Syndicate would not be all too willing to share nothing, but if some outside Reality Deviant comes with some fresh and solid Intel, they wouldn't refuse. And they wouldn't so much &quot;share Intel&quot; with them, as so much as &quot;look, if a certain factory were to be blown away, it would be very interesting to both of us&quot;. They wouldn't explain why, but they would just try to direct these monsters in the direction they want.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-15T10:52:29-07:00","id":1540439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540162-hypothetically-what-aid-could-the-syndicate-give-to-others-in-destroying-pentex?p=1540324#post1540324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But the most glaring problem with this certainty about Syndicate victory: this is all true in a Mage game. It isn't all that clearcut in a game centered on another splat.<br /> <br /> If this is, as it seems to be the case, a WtA game, then the Technocracy is just a thing, not <b>THE </b>thing. The enemy is the Wyrm and, while not its direct servant, Pentex is the best agent of utter corruption at playing corporate conspiracy games.<br /> <br /> Nefandi are also probably a far more common thing than in the average Mage game, and even in Mage the dept of their presence within Technocratic ranks is unknown, which is another problem the Syndicate may face: it's not just those 10%.</div> </div> </div> </div>That much is indeed true. In a WtA game, that balance is indeed, not so certain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-15T12:15:20-07:00","id":1540449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540162-hypothetically-what-aid-could-the-syndicate-give-to-others-in-destroying-pentex?p=1540438#post1540438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. Despite (probably) being a problem that the Syndicate can deal with and (perhaps) contain, the Pentex IS dangerous. I was mentioning the &quot;institutional&quot; pathways that it could use to strike back, should it saw itself being cornered. Besides those there are, quite obviously, many pathways to go into that are out of the use of societal institutions - crime and supernatural means, such as Fomori, are some of those.<br /> <br /> Pentex also has allies outside of their ranks, and potential allies, such as other Wyrm servants.<br /> <br /> For all of these reasons AND the need for keeping things rush-rush, is why the Syndicate would take baby steps towards that threat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, if the Syndicate member is close to the EFD of the VE, they might get some epic backfires if they ask for physical/military backup. The EFD, you see, uses what they don't realize are fomori for security in their deep sea operations... I guess it's not just one methodology that's corrupted, at the end of the day. (see: Blood-Dimmed Tides)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sure, the Syndicate would not be all too willing to share nothing, but if some outside Reality Deviant comes with some fresh and solid Intel, they wouldn't refuse. And they wouldn't so much &quot;share Intel&quot; with them, as so much as &quot;look, if a certain factory were to be blown away, it would be very interesting to both of us&quot;. They wouldn't explain why, but they would just try to direct these monsters in the direction they want. </div> </div> </div>But why? By all indications, the Syndicate is extremely paranoid and shares the TU's tendency to shoot first and never ask questions, because they don't care about the answer that you're giving. Greed is good and this is progress, baby! Now where's my chemical focus for Time? I've got a methodology to manage! [Sounds of Syndicate member snorting a huge line of coke]<br /> <br /> It'd have to be individuals doing this strictly off the books, and correct me if I'm wrong, but they'd be risking a trip to the corrective re-brainwashing division of the TU if they were coordinating with any kind of Reality Deviant. The amount of help that the actual institution would give, therefore, would be &quot;none&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-15T17:35:26-07:00","id":1540481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540162-hypothetically-what-aid-could-the-syndicate-give-to-others-in-destroying-pentex?p=1540449#post1540449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, if the Syndicate member is close to the EFD of the VE, they might get some epic backfires if they ask for physical/military backup. The EFD, you see, uses what they don't realize are fomori for security in their deep sea operations... I guess it's not just one methodology that's corrupted, at the end of the day. (see: Blood-Dimmed Tides)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> But why? By all indications, the Syndicate is extremely paranoid and shares the TU's tendency to shoot first and never ask questions, because they don't care about the answer that you're giving. Greed is good and this is progress, baby! Now where's my chemical focus for Time? I've got a methodology to manage! [Sounds of Syndicate member snorting a huge line of coke]<br /> <br /> It'd have to be individuals doing this strictly off the books, and correct me if I'm wrong, but they'd be risking a trip to the corrective re-brainwashing division of the TU if they were coordinating with any kind of Reality Deviant. The amount of help that the actual institution would give, therefore, would be &quot;none&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Syndicate is more willing to deal amicably with RDs, as long as it doesn't bring problems, that much I can give them.<br /> <br /> But I agree that the institution as a whole isn't likely to offer much help, or react well to any demonstration that you have evidence of their blunder.<br /> <br /> Everything here is, IC, secrets within the Convention that not everyone knows and a lot of people are acting upon with utmost care and secrecy. And however real it is, the Syndicate is sure that they can deal with this problem with time, that their way is better, and that liabilities must be eliminated.<br /> <br /> Getting help is possible, but you have to first prove you're not a liability, they won't simply accept any help before they're sure they covered their bases. And even then you need to present very good info.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-15T19:33:52-07:00","id":1540495,"title":"","content":"I think it's plausible that the Syndicate could officially end up at cross purposes with Pentex, if it's approached right. Assuming that this is not a scenario with Nephandic infiltration, then the Technocracy has a vested interest in the world existing and being a relatively safe (and profitable) place. If they became aware that this wasn't exactly Pentex's endgame, and the extent of that, they might be willing to act.<br /> <br /> If approached right, of course, but that's for the player characters to figure out.<br /> <br /> As to which one would win, it'd probably depend on which kind of game we're playing. In a Mage game with Werewolf elements, I think the Syndicate's got a pretty good shot. After all, a fight with the Syndicate is a fight with the Technocracy on a whole. So while there's Fomori on one side, there's Hit Marks, Victors, and Void Engineer weaponry on the other. Both are global entities, but Pentex is one corporation while the Technocracy has its tendrils pretty much everywhere.<br /> <br /> In a Werewolf game with Mage elements, then Pentex isn't just a powerful corporation with Umbral ties but a tool of one of the Triat. A Syndicate/Technocracy victory might still be possible (especially if you read them as tools of the Weaver), but I wouldn't expect more than a pyrrhic victory, and more likely it'd be the Syndicate going down (perhaps with a surprisingly noble last stand, or maybe not.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2430,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","user":"kalinara","date":". 08-15-2024, 10:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-17T11:58:53-07:00","id":1540581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalinara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540162-hypothetically-what-aid-could-the-syndicate-give-to-others-in-destroying-pentex?p=1540495#post1540495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's plausible that the Syndicate could officially end up at cross purposes with Pentex, if it's approached right. <b>Assuming that this is not a scenario with Nephandic infiltration</b>, then the Technocracy has a vested interest in the world existing and being a relatively safe (and profitable) place. If they became aware that this wasn't exactly Pentex's endgame, and the extent of that, they might be willing to act.</div> </div> </div> </div>(Looks at EFD and SPD)<br /> <br /> That... might not be a safe assumption.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If approached right, of course, but that's for the player characters to figure out. </div> </div> </div>That generally seems to be on course for most crazy stuff in the WoD. If it's at odds with the authority, it probably rests with the PCs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As to which one would win, it'd probably depend on which kind of game we're playing. In a Mage game with Werewolf elements, I think the Syndicate's got a pretty good shot. After all, a fight with the Syndicate is a fight with the Technocracy on a whole. So while there's Fomori on one side, there's Hit Marks, Victors, and Void Engineer weaponry on the other. Both are global entities, but Pentex is one corporation while the Technocracy has its tendrils pretty much everywhere. </div> </div> </div>Congratulations, Pentex has you playing the same game that they have the Garou playing. All your cool guns and rad killer cyborgs are tied up fighting enemies that they can just pop right back out because they rely on Human Resources, which they can keep popping out faster than you can replace your cool guns, highly trained ops, and rad killer cyborgs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In a Werewolf game with Mage elements, then Pentex isn't just a powerful corporation with Umbral ties but a tool of one of the Triat. A Syndicate/Technocracy victory might still be possible (especially if you read them as tools of the Weaver), but I wouldn't expect more than a pyrrhic victory, and more likely it'd be the Syndicate going down (perhaps with a surprisingly noble last stand, or maybe not.) </div> </div> </div>The Weaver has little to no defense against the Defiler. It slides along the webs without the Weaver's knowledge and bends it toward its own ends; that is, in fact, its thing. A pyrrhic victory might be out of the entire TU's grasp, as they experience the attention that the Garou have been suffering under for generations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-17T16:55:55-07:00","id":1540596,"title":"","content":"I think the degree to which the Technocracy can be effective against PENTEX relies heavily on the degree to which it can play nice with the &quot;Reality Deviants&quot; who were already fighting it. The Technocracy is really poorly suited to handle the Wyrm because they don't understand the Umbra. Their cosmology posits that the Umbra is just a the products of instinctual thought (human or otherwise) rather than fundamentally interlinked with the material world. This renders them unable to see how events in the Umbra will influence events in the material world <i>even if</i> no spirits (oh, sorry, &quot;EDEs&quot;) cross over and prohibits them from recognizing that things that happen to nonthinking beings still have effects in the Umbra even if no creature with instinct notices them. In all likelihood they would ignore much of PENTEX's work because it shouldn't have any particularly harmful effect--and if they recognize that it does, they're liable to be reprogrammed because the Union regards animism as reality deviancy even though it is objectively true.<br /> <br /> This aside, even in scenarios where the Garou are largely unaware of PENTEX, they have more experience fighting the group than the Technocracy does. The Technocracy would be going in without any intelligence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-18T11:21:54-07:00","id":1540639,"title":"","content":"The only thing in this whole debacle that plays more or less in favor of the Garou (assuming we're talking Garou here), is that in general fighting them is very low on the Union's priorities.<br /> <br /> Werewolf usually clean their own messes, and the Union doesn't like to waste resources battling people who clean their messes.<br /> <br /> If the Garou aren't the kind to cause too much problems or human casualties, they can expect to be actually heard by the Syndicate instead of shot down. It would be a very risky conversation, but would at least start as a conversation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-19T10:22:00-07:00","id":1540712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540162-hypothetically-what-aid-could-the-syndicate-give-to-others-in-destroying-pentex?p=1540449#post1540449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, if the Syndicate member is close to the EFD of the VE, they might get some epic backfires if they ask for physical/military backup. The EFD, you see, uses what they don't realize are fomori for security in their deep sea operations... I guess it's not just one methodology that's corrupted, at the end of the day. (see: Blood-Dimmed Tides)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the VE have their own Nefandic issues to deal with.<br /> <br /> But the Syndicate will not be asking them for help.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But why? By all indications, the Syndicate is extremely paranoid and shares the TU's tendency to shoot first and never ask questions, because they don't care about the answer that you're giving. Greed is good and this is progress, baby! Now where's my chemical focus for Time? I've got a methodology to manage! [Sounds of Syndicate member snorting a huge line of coke]<br /> <br /> It'd have to be individuals doing this strictly off the books, and correct me if I'm wrong, but they'd be risking a trip to the corrective re-brainwashing division of the TU if they were coordinating with any kind of Reality Deviant. The amount of help that the actual institution would give, therefore, would be &quot;none&quot;. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540162-hypothetically-what-aid-could-the-syndicate-give-to-others-in-destroying-pentex?p=1540481#post1540481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Syndicate is more willing to deal amicably with RDs, as long as it doesn't bring problems, that much I can give them.<br /> <br /> But I agree that the institution as a whole isn't likely to offer much help, or react well to any demonstration that you have evidence of their blunder.<br /> <br /> Everything here is, IC, secrets within the Convention that not everyone knows and a lot of people are acting upon with utmost care and secrecy. And however real it is, the Syndicate is sure that they can deal with this problem with time, that their way is better, and that liabilities must be eliminated.<br /> <br /> Getting help is possible, but you have to first prove you're not a liability, they won't simply accept any help before they're sure they covered their bases. And even then you need to present very good info.</div> </div> </div> </div>This right here. It isn't so much so that the Techie boys are &quot;techno-barbarians&quot; filled with berserker rage towards all RDs. They can make arrangements and find compromises when it fulfills their purposes - the Union is not stupid after all. But whatever kind of deal that can be arranged must have a potential net positive result for their agendas and preferably with minimum collaterals. It is therefore just hard to make alliances with the techies, which makes them rare, but not impossible. Just remember that, whatever alliance will only ever be temporary (unless you as a Reality Deviant were willing to put on a &quot;slave collar&quot; around your neck that will turn you into an automaton servant) and they'll most likely get back on the business of hunting you down as soon as their objectives are met, and that whatever kind of deal you make with them will always be for their benefit above your own. You can still acquire benefits from such an alliance thou, it's just that they'll get MORE out of it (although that is relative. How much would it be worth for the Syndicate to completely eliminate Pentex? A lot, let's be real here, it would be one of the things that their hearts most desire. But on the other hand, how much more would it be worth it for the Garou? Perhaps even more. So yes, it is possible to have win-win bargains).<br /> <br /> Just for the sake of Gaia, don't give them reasons to see you as a liability rather than an asset, and you should be good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-19T10:35:27-07:00","id":1540713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Citrakayah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540162-hypothetically-what-aid-could-the-syndicate-give-to-others-in-destroying-pentex?p=1540596#post1540596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the degree to which the Technocracy can be effective against PENTEX relies heavily on the degree to which it can play nice with the &quot;Reality Deviants&quot; who were already fighting it. The Technocracy is really poorly suited to handle the Wyrm because they don't understand the Umbra. Their cosmology posits that the Umbra is just a the products of instinctual thought (human or otherwise) rather than fundamentally interlinked with the material world. This renders them unable to see how events in the Umbra will influence events in the material world <i>even if</i> no spirits (oh, sorry, &quot;EDEs&quot;) cross over and prohibits them from recognizing that things that happen to nonthinking beings still have effects in the Umbra even if no creature with instinct notices them. In all likelihood they would ignore much of PENTEX's work because it shouldn't have any particularly harmful effect--and if they recognize that it does, they're liable to be reprogrammed because the Union regards animism as reality deviancy even though it is objectively true.<br /> <br /> This aside, even in scenarios where the Garou are largely unaware of PENTEX, they have more experience fighting the group than the Technocracy does. The Technocracy would be going in without any intelligence.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the problem thou, Animism is &quot;objectively true&quot; in a Werewolf game, but NOT in a Mage game.<br /> <br /> Werewolf Umbra is objective; Mage's Umbra is not, is subjective.<br /> <br /> Which is why all of this is reliant on from which side are we looking at things.<br /> <br /> And like Momteparnas said, the Garou are really very low on the &quot;to do&quot; list of the Union. Bellow superstitious &quot;Mages&quot;, Nephandic and Crazy entities, even bellow vampires, and the bloodsuckers already are low in their list too.<br /> <br /> So, the Union will one day want to get rid of the Garou... But only after all the rest.<br /> <br /> Therefore, they would be willing to listen.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, one good alternative for the players would be to seek out the NWO instead of the Syndicate. These guys would REALLY be interested in hear the RDs... But that could cost the players an eternal burning hatred from the Syndicate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-19T23:48:29-07:00","id":1540752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540162-hypothetically-what-aid-could-the-syndicate-give-to-others-in-destroying-pentex?p=1540713#post1540713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's the problem thou, Animism is &quot;objectively true&quot; in a Werewolf game, but NOT in a Mage game.<br /> <br /> Werewolf Umbra is objective; Mage's Umbra is not, is subjective.<br /> <br /> Which is why all of this is reliant on from which side are we looking at things.<br /> <br /> And like Momteparnas said, the Garou are really very low on the &quot;to do&quot; list of the Union. Bellow superstitious &quot;Mages&quot;, Nephandic and Crazy entities, even bellow vampires, and the bloodsuckers already are low in their list too.<br /> <br /> So, the Union will one day want to get rid of the Garou... But only after all the rest.<br /> <br /> Therefore, they would be willing to listen.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, one good alternative for the players would be to seek out the NWO instead of the Syndicate. These guys would REALLY be interested in hear the RDs... But that could cost the players an eternal burning hatred from the Syndicate.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're using Pentex, you're getting down, down into Werewolf-town, so it's not really much of a stretch to just go the rest of the way. I doubt that the NWO would be that much more enthusiastic to help Garou and/or Fera, though, Syndicate rivalry or not. Their philosophy is going to make them seem one step away from succumbing to OneSong, and likewise, the Rage of the Garou and Fera is going to likely be deemed an unacceptable personality flaw in operations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just for the sake of Gaia, don't give them reasons to see you as a liability rather than an asset, and you should be good. </div> </div> </div>&quot;That's my secret, Cap. I'm always going to be a liability to the Syndicate; my values are at odds with corporate enterprise and can't coexist with them.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-20T15:19:05-07:00","id":1540805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540162-hypothetically-what-aid-could-the-syndicate-give-to-others-in-destroying-pentex?p=1540752#post1540752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> &quot;That's my secret, Cap. I'm always going to be a liability to the Syndicate; my values are at odds with corporate enterprise and can't coexist with them.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but there's a difference between being an immediate liability and a long term liability. And the Syndicate is officially the second most likely Convention to work with RDs.<br /> <br /> Sure, that would demand a special kind of Werewolf to be an asset to the Syndicate in the foreseeable future. But that's what PCs are for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-15T08:48:27-07:00","id":1553201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540162-hypothetically-what-aid-could-the-syndicate-give-to-others-in-destroying-pentex?p=1540713#post1540713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's the problem thou, Animism is &quot;objectively true&quot; in a Werewolf game, but NOT in a Mage game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. Spirit 3's ability to awaken dormant spirits in objects makes animism objectively true in Mage. The Technocracy doesn't believe a lot of things which are objectively true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26432-jagnestormskull","name":"JagneStormskull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26432_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-15T12:56:14-07:00","id":1553210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JagneStormskull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540162-hypothetically-what-aid-could-the-syndicate-give-to-others-in-destroying-pentex?p=1553201#post1553201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I disagree. Spirit 3's ability to awaken dormant spirits in objects makes animism objectively true in Mage. The Technocracy doesn't believe a lot of things which are objectively true.</div> </div> </div> </div>That all depends on what you mean by &quot;Animism&quot;.<br /> <br /> Other dimensions objectively exist and are inhabited. Objects are linked to dormant entities that can be awaken to affect them. And the Technocracy does know all of that, there isn't anything at all that is objectively true that the Union doesn't believe (although there may be particular Agents that don't believe, but that's also true for any Mage).<br /> <br /> What isn't objectively true is the role of those dimensions in reality and their cosmology implications. The true nature of a spirit and what they mean to reality isn't by any means objective or verifiable in Mage, at least not in a way that wouldn't accommodate to your Paradigm to begin with.<br /> <br /> So... the Syndicate would be at least somewhat prepared to deal with the spiritual aspects anyway. There <b>would</b> be communication issues between Garou and Syndicate, but nothing insurmountable (especially compared to all the other issues between them). At the same time, which game you take as right about the cosmology for this game does make a difference, and I'm with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> here to an extent. While I don't think it impossible to run this completely under Mage assumptions, the whole plot is extremely Werewolf-adjacent since its inception in Mage, I'd say even without Garou getting involved this begs for the Wyrm flavor of Nefandus and the full nine yards of Wyrm minions, agents, goals, everything. It doesn't have to objectively deny Mage's usual assumptions, but they'd be a completely unnecessary burden.<br /> <br /> Add to that that the Syndicate is already the most Earth-bound Convention, with little interest or theoretical framework for the Umbra. So we're not, to begin with, talking about a Convention that'll have a Theory of Umbra to conflict with the Garou's, and would actually probably defer most of it to their &quot;contracted specialists&quot;. They know their stuff, good, how much it's based on superstition is completely irrelevant, and they could be actually right for all I care.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}